A||||3||Phantom Rage||V6 Timing Question||||1||
Z||000000||Phantom Rage||03-12-2000||02:28 PM||||How do you properly time an 88-v6 motor if the distributor was taken out and crank moved?<P>1) There seems to be 3 slits on the wheel behind the crank pulley.  <P>    a) Are those the marks I need to align with the "0" degree mark?<P>    b) If so Which one.<P>2) Is the number one spark plug (looking from the rear of the car) the last one on the right?<P>3) When the number one piston is at it's very top in the cylinder, is it in the compression stroke.<P>4) Where do I align the base of the distributor?<P>5) Where do I align the rotor?  My Hanes manual says between cylinders 1 and 6 on the cap.  <P>    a) If so then to which side? (Clockwise 90 deg. from 6 or clock wise 90deg. from 1)<P>Thx||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||03-12-2000||11:16 PM||||<BR>a) Are those the marks I need to align with the "0" degree mark?<BR>YES<BR>b) If so Which one.<BR>I THINK THE MIDDLE ONE<BR>2) Is the number one spark plug (looking from the rear of the car) the last one on the right?<BR>NUMBER 1 IS RIGHT SIDE TOWARDS REAR OF CAR<P>3) When the number one piston is at it's very top in the cylinder, is it in the compression stroke.<BR>THERE ARE 2 UP STROKES COMPRESSION AND EXHAUST.<BR>THE BEST WAY TO TELL IS #1 AT TOP OF CYLINDER, TIMING MARK AT 0, AND BOTH VALVES CLOSED. THIS IS THE COMPRESSION STROKE. YOU CAN USE A COMPRESSION TESTER GAGE TO SEE WHEN CYLINDER IS COMPRESSING THEN SET CRANK TO 0 DEGREES. (OR REMOVE VAVLE COVER)<BR>4) Where do I align the base of the distributor?<BR>ALIGN DITRIBUTOR SO YOU HAVE ROOM TO MOVE IT LEFT AND RIGHT WITH THE WIRE HARNESS CONNECTORS ON IT. GENNERALLY ABOUT 225 DEGREES FROM FRONT OF CAR.<BR>5) Where do I align the rotor? My Hanes manual says between cylinders 1 and 6 on the cap. <BR>THE ROTOR WILL TURN CLOCKWISE WHEN INSERTING DISTRIBUTOR. TO GET TIMING CLOSE ENOUGH FOR THE ENGINE TO RUN YOU WANT THE ROTOR TO BE WHERE THE #1 OF THE CAP IS. SO INSERT IT WHERE THE ROTOR POINTS INBETWEEN 6 AND 1 MAKING SURE ONCE DISTRIBUTOR IS ALL THE WAY SEATED IT POINTS TO #1.<P>Sorry about using caps for the answers, I just thought this would be an easy way to answer many questions on the same post.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phantom Rage||03-13-2000||04:31 PM||||Hey, thx Oreif.<BR>Was waiting for a reply all night, finally fell asleep.<P>I was refering to the wheel on the crankshaft, next to the crankshaft pulley.  It has three slits in it, I know you said the middle one, but its round so where do I start?  One of them has some paint on it, maybe from the factory, or some mechanic.  May that's it.<P>Is the valve cover gasket, one of those neoprean ones or are they cork ones?  <P>Thx again Oreif, or to anyone else!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||03-13-2000||05:08 PM||||1- On my car one of the three marks is obviously wider than the other tow. Check it out.<BR>2- Take #1 plug out, stuck your finger in hard and crank engine until you feel air pressure out. If cranking with starter do very small cranks. Once you feel the preasure look for that wide slit and align it with 0 mark. Easiest way is to use ratchet and turn pulley until aligned. I think it is a 15mm to 18mm.<BR>5- Easiest for this is to try to align the rotor in a way that when it points to a cap contact the flat base of it is pointing towards 7 o clock position. That conector will be your #1 plug wire. Connect number 1 wire to that an clockwise connect 2,3.. until 6 wire.<BR>Before tightening rotate cap counter clockwise (advance) a little more than 1/4 inch. This will advance it a little so it start up better. After that time it and you are on the go.||||reg||1
